1
00:05:07,586 --> 00:05:10,700
Oh, that's very charming, but...

2
00:05:11,333 --> 00:05:16,535
- Lieutenant Anderson.
- Lieutenant Anderson, of course.

3
00:05:17,048 --> 00:05:20,636
Chief of detectives of the Zenith police
department, This is Miss Allen.

4
00:05:20,666 --> 00:05:22,355
- Miss Allen.
- How do you do?

5
00:05:22,385 --> 00:05:26,786
Lt. Anderson is one of our favorite citizens,
he's on the Bank's board of directors.

6
00:05:27,481 --> 00:05:30,812
- Not bad for a policeman.
- You must've made a good thing of it.

7
00:05:32,124 --> 00:05:34,362
Well, I saved my money,
if that's what you mean.

8
00:05:34,392 --> 00:05:38,517
It's near closing time and I've got some
business in the safe deposit vault.

9
00:05:39,135 --> 00:05:41,366
- Please come and see me Miss Bailey.
- Oh, I'd love to.

10
00:05:41,396 --> 00:05:42,573
- And you Lieutenant.
- Thank you.

11
00:05:42,603 --> 00:05:44,940
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye, nice to have met you.

12
00:05:46,704 --> 00:05:50,624
My, what a charming woman, she
moved into the Oaks just the other day.

13
00:05:51,559 --> 00:05:53,835
That house is a proper
sitting for a writer of mysteries.

14
00:05:53,865 --> 00:05:56,006
Oh, it certainly is.

15
00:05:58,448 --> 00:06:02,503
- Dick, what's the matter?
- Come in here, both of you.

16
00:06:08,745 --> 00:06:11,355
Andy, we're in trouble.
Wendell Hynes came

17
00:06:11,379 --> 00:06:14,308
in to pick up $350,000
worth of bonds that...

18
00:06:14,487 --> 00:06:16,615
we were holding as collateral for a loan.

19
00:06:17,172 --> 00:06:18,906
They were kept in our special vault.

20
00:06:19,222 --> 00:06:23,021
Mr. Fleming and I are the only officers
of the bank who have access to that vault.

21
00:06:23,051 --> 00:06:26,323
- So?
- The Hynes bonds are gone.

22
00:06:27,122 --> 00:06:30,650
That's not all, other
negotiable securities are missing.

23
00:06:31,041 --> 00:06:33,348
From what I can gather
short of a careful check...

24
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:37,238
the bank is been looted of over
a million dollars worth of securities.

25
00:06:37,615 --> 00:06:39,258
You'll have to notify Fleming.

26
00:06:40,313 --> 00:06:44,942
I wish I could talk to him. Unfortunately,
he and Dr. Wells are deep in the woods.

27
00:06:45,740 --> 00:06:47,640
They can't be reached by phone.

28
00:07:00,091 --> 00:07:01,161
What is it?

29
00:07:09,769 --> 00:07:12,437
I thought I heard someone
on the path coming from the lake.

30
00:07:12,467 --> 00:07:14,379
Had an idea it might
be that guide of ours.

31
00:07:14,403 --> 00:07:16,269
Oh, Sam won't
show up until morning.

32
00:07:16,299 --> 00:07:18,979
It's a 20 mile canoe trip
from here to civilization.

33
00:07:19,696 --> 00:07:22,591
Five will get you 10,
Sam has a message for me.

34
00:07:22,984 --> 00:07:25,346
I thought you told them at
the bank not to bother you.

35
00:07:25,508 --> 00:07:27,692
I did, but they'll bother me.

36
00:07:30,981 --> 00:07:33,003
- Doctor?
- Yes, John.

37
00:07:34,254 --> 00:07:36,484
What would you do for half a million?

38
00:07:37,503 --> 00:07:39,085
Anything short of murder.

39
00:07:40,089 --> 00:07:41,069
Why not murder?

40
00:07:42,327 --> 00:07:43,084
Too messy.

41
00:07:43,739 --> 00:07:44,766
Too great a risk?

42
00:07:44,974 --> 00:07:46,580
For half a million? Yes.

43
00:07:48,385 --> 00:07:50,438
I pinched a million from the bank.

44
00:07:52,523 --> 00:07:53,581
I'm not kidding.

45
00:07:54,376 --> 00:07:55,287
I embezzled it.

46
00:07:56,337 --> 00:07:59,439
Not that I think you wouldn't do it
if you thought you could get away with it.

47
00:08:00,697 --> 00:08:01,886
I got away with it.

48
00:08:02,981 --> 00:08:05,058
I'm not talking about currency.

49
00:08:05,930 --> 00:08:09,303
I took negotiable securities that
could be converted into cash.

50
00:08:10,106 --> 00:08:13,757
I have the cash, in tens,
twenties, and hundreds.

51
00:08:14,636 --> 00:08:17,284
And I'm your doctor,
not your lawyer, why tell me this?
